From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:28:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(shares): never ask for an anonymous share

All three ways of sharing a folder (the file browser's context menu,
the "Shared Folders" guide and "share" in the new-folder dialog) posted
anonymous: true. The root service refuses anonymous shares (mandatory
SMB signing; guest access is off), so sharing a folder from the
dashboard always failed with that error. They now ask for an
authenticated share, the only kind there is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
